1
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:23,900
kicking a pebble, flying off on a bear.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,160
The joking type,
always clowning around, Kashibari.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
They laughed at me for
staying as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:38,680
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
all I can do is win.

6
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:43,880
One nightmare, and the unchanging
streets are gentler still.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:48,720
The crows are calling,
so the day is already ending.

8
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,860
Are you going to watch me
stuff yakitori in my cheeks?

9
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:11,080
Thank you for watching.

10
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:36,100
Ugh, damn it,
we're not catching a damn thing!

11
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,220
I came here because I heard
the fish were biting nonstop.

12
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,080
Hey, fisherman, are you catching any?

13
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:42,500
Nothing at all!

14
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,220
At this rate, we might go without dinner

15
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,180
Ahaha, well, what do we have here!

16
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:50,960
Hey, senpai, something's floating this way!

17
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:53,480
What the hell is that?

18
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:02,520
That's a strange shape for a coconut.

19
00:02:03,380 --> 00:02:08,400
Hey, Sechi-senpai, that's,
that's a Gomu Gomu no Mi!

20
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:15,040
Gomu Gomu no Mi? What's that supposed to be?

21
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:16,960
You don't know?

22
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:22,600
It's a legendary fruit that makes your body
stretch and shrink like rubber when you eat it.

23
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:26,760
Don't give me that manga nonsense.
Something like that couldn't possibly exist.

24
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,020
It's true.

25
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:32,820
It looks exactly like the fruit from One Piece,
the manga everyone's crazy about right now.

26
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:34,620
That's just from a manga!

27
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,820
Anyway, let's make this our dinner tonight.

28
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:38,920
Senpai...

29
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,300
Itadakimasu.

30
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:43,840
It tastes kind of weird.

31
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,800
Don't blame me if something happens.

32
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:49,760
Can we really do this?

33
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:03,160
Shut up already.

34
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:08,020
You bastard.

35
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:11,500
It hurts.

36
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,540
What the hell is going on?

37
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:19,140
Mm?

38
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,640
Mm?

39
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:55,640
Senpai?

40
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:56,720
Get out of the way!

41
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:01,540
Senpai!

42
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:09,740
I'm fine!

43
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:13,280
Senpai, you really became a rubber man!

44
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:16,180
Shut up! It's your fault!

45
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:18,380
Why didn't you stop me back then?

46
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:22,420
I tried to stop you,
but you ate it anyway, didn't you?

47
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:22,720
Clang!

48
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,680
Hey, forget about all that now.

49
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:28,440
Honda, get a doctor. Hurry to the hospital.

50
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:29,100
Yes!

51
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:31,400
Let's go, Boss Ryotsu!

52
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,840
Alright, express speed!

53
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,600
Alright!

54
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,520
Let's take a closer look!

55
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,680
Whoa!

56
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:40,800
Uiii, gowaaaaah!

57
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,000
What's wrong, Boss Ryotsu?

58
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,000
Hey, boss!

59
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,260
Okay, here we go!

60
00:04:50,260 --> 00:05:06,560
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

61
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,760
Right, I'm saving you now!

62
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,240
What is this, seriously now...

63
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,400
Oh no!

64
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,960
How can you swim?

65
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:25,320
Did your body turn into rubber?

66
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,340
Yeah, it did.

67
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:31,800
When I woke up this morning, my arms
were stretching and shrinking like rubber.

68
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,400
I can't believe something that ridiculous,
like it's out of a comic book.

69
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:42,860
Whoa!

70
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:45,220
It really is stretching!

71
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:48,980
It's not just your arms.
Nakagawa, I'm going to pull your leg.

72
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:49,960
Yes.

73
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,640
Huh?

74
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,180
Idiot, don't just suddenly talk!

75
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:01,200
I'm not used to handling it yet.

76
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,480
Be careful.

77
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:04,900
Understood.

78
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:06,880
But if your legs stretch too,

79
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:08,620
does your neck and face stretch as well?

80
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,100
Like this.

81
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:13,940
Thanks to that,
I ended up nearly drowning in the river.

82
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:15,960
With a body like this,

83
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,840
I can't even walk outside properly.

84
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,140
But how did you end up
with a body like that?

85
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:29,100
Senpai, you ate a fruit called the Gomu Gomu no Mi that you found at sea yesterday,
and that's why you became a rubber man.

86
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:34,660
My hands, feet, neck,
and face all stretch out now.

87
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:41,160
Well, you've split into two
and turned into six before, so

88
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:43,700
you've still got a ridiculous body, I see.

89
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:47,220
You two should show a little concern!
Why did this happen to me?

90
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:49,660
Bakabon!

91
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:52,820
It's because you've been living
a sloppy life all the time.

92
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:54,440
That's why you end up with a body like that.

93
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,920
How about eating some fruit you picked
up from the sea and turning into a freak?

94
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,220
You brought it on yourself.

95
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:02,740
Can't you, you big idiot,
live a decent life for once?

96
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:06,140
Stop it, Chief!

97
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:08,600
So, Honda-san,

98
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,040
is there no way to change me back?

99
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:14,040
Apparently, no one has found one yet.

100
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,780
What?

101
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:18,660
So does that mean I'll be a
rubber man for the rest of my life?

102
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:19,980
Hey.

103
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:22,680
Do you think a few words will settle this?

104
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,060
Stop it, senpai, this leg...

105
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:28,880
Don't take it out on Honda.
It's your own fault.

106
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:33,640
Since I'm a rubber man,
I don't feel it even when I'm hit.

107
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,820
Preposterous!

108
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:40,020
That's why, with this strange body,
I'm exhausted,

109
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:42,280
so I'm going to leave early today.

110
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,380
What nonsense are you talking?

111
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,060
Do you think an excuse
like that will be allowed?

112
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:50,360
Come on,
what's the harm in taking one day off?

113
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:53,080
Dai-da

114
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:59,940
If you have time to rest, then think of ways to put that strange
power of yours to use for the good of the world and its people.

115
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:02,200
For the good of the world and its people.

116
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:06,140
Yeah, if you use it well, it might
be pretty handy in all sorts of ways.

117
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:10,360
If you're going to put that body to use,
I won't complain.

118
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,840
Really, Chief?

119
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:16,700
Alright, from today I'm the Gomu
Gomu territory management officer!

120
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:24,300


121
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,660
I'm still not used to this body, you know!

122
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:32,600
Please, give me a little more time,
would you?

123
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,460
Give me time.

124
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:38,560
Don't talk nonsense.

125
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:48,480
We did it, big brother!

126
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,940
Now we're rich too!

127
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:52,500
Let's get out of here fast!

128
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,000
That's far enough!

129
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:54,400
Coming out!

130
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:01,640
You can't run anymore!

131
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,960
Be a good boy and hand over your wrists.

132
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:07,040
What can you possibly do from up there?

133
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,640
Did you think we'd wait
for you to come down here?

134
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,580
No, we won't make you wait!

135
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:13,700
Yaah!

136
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,000
What?

137
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,340
Do you think big brother's dead?

138
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:23,020
There's no way he survived
a fall from that height...

139
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:36,120
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

140
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:59,340
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

141
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:02,180
Never mind us, just floor it!

142
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:03,820
Nnn.

143
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,500
You're number one.

144
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:23,800
I'm the mass-produced Gomu Gomu!

145
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:47,200
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

146
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,760
Somebody, help!

147
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,340
The fire's spread that far already!

148
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:52,640
Where's the fire truck? Is it still coming?

149
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,120
Leave it to me!

150
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,200
Gabu Gabu race!

151
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,680
Okay, we're safe now. Let's run!

152
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:10,800
But the fire's already right there...

153
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:11,620
What?

154
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:15,340
We don't need to go through the room!

155
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,920
It's fine! I'm not dead!

156
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,500
Hmph! I'm not dead!

157
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,560
Gomu Gomu rescue complete!

158
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:35,340
Senpai, that's amazing!
Your achievements are all here!

159
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:37,840
Nahaha! Of course!

160
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:40,484
After all, thanks to becoming a rubber man,

161
00:11:40,534 --> 00:11:43,800
you're fine even when you're
hit or run over by a car!

162
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:49,660
Plus, by using the rubber's momentum, your punches
and kicks are several times stronger than usual.

163
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:52,380
Once you get used to it,
you won't find a more convenient ability.

164
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:55,580
As expected of Ryo-chan,
such amazing adaptability.

165
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,080
Ryotsu, well done.

166
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:02,540
Actually, it's been decided that you'll be
receiving the Police Commissioner's Commendation soon.

167
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,640
Really, Chief?

168
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:06,760
Of course.

169
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:10,720
You've been working for the good of the world and its people,
just as I told you to.

170
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,520
There's nothing happier than this, Ryotsu.

171
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:15,640
Chief, Chief.

172
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,560
Keep it up like this from now on, all right?

173
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:21,280
Yes, of course.

174
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,754
Since I've gained this power,

175
00:12:23,804 --> 00:12:26,320
I'll put it to use for everyone.

176
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,540
Oof, there we go.

177
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:41,340
Well, once you get used to it,
this body is pretty handy.

178
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:46,840
I can reach things far away
even while sitting down,

179
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:53,980
but I can't grab the snacks that are already gone,
of course.

180
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:56,240
Should I go to the convenience store?

181
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,100
But I also want to watch TV.

182
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:01,400
I know!

183
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,100
Aaaaaaah!

184
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:48,740
Eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh
eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh eh, eh

185
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:55,400
Where's the territory, the territory?

186
00:13:56,320 --> 00:14:04,180
Well, I haven't seen it at all since this morning, but what?
I told you so many times to deliver the paperwork today!

187
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:09,000
Whoa!

188
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:15,500
The paperwork I asked for, the one for 4...
that was just now.

189
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,020
Yes, this is Kōen-mae.

190
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,140
Ryo-chan.

191
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,940
You saw what just happened, didn't you?

192
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:29,560
Since I found out that if I just stretch my arms,
I can get things done without moving around.

193
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,500
From today on,
I've decided to work from home.

194
00:14:33,640 --> 00:14:34,840
You idiot!

195
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,880
Do you think such irresponsible
behavior should be allowed?

196
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:40,140
Get your face over to
the station right away.

197
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:42,400
Understood, then I'll just...

198
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,060
"Then I'll just" what?

199
00:14:45,500 --> 00:15:04,980
Ohhh, what a relief,


200
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:07,780
Hurry up and bring your body over here!

201
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,780
No, Chief, you can't pull me that hard!

202
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:18,220
That's exactly why I told you not to!

203
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:20,840
You idiot, let go of me quickly!

204
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:26,680
What is this?

205
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:32,020
What the hell?

206
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:33,700
Excuse me!

207
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:34,900
Senpai!

208
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,260
Boinging around like that is dangerous,
you know!

209
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:41,400
Ryo-chan's working from home, you know.

210
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:44,320
He's doing great with his Gomu Gomu powers.

211
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:47,200
They're letting him get away
with a little selfishness.

212
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:50,520
But can he really get any work done at home?

213
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,140
Nakagawa!

214
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,900
Don't think I won't know
right away if you badmouth me!

215
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,340
W-where is Senpai?

216
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,720
Nakagawa, over there.

217
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,900
There.

218
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:05,560
With this camera, I can monitor everything
going on at the station from my room.

219
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,140
So working from home is no problem.

220
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:11,840
This way,
he can be late as much as he likes.

221
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:14,260
Gomu Gomu really does come in handy,
doesn't it.

222
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:20,000
Senpai, you're using your powers wrong.

223
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:23,720
At this rate, he's not Gomu Gomu,
he's Dara Dara Ryo-chan

224
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,300
Good morning, everyone.

225
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:27,920
Good morning.

226
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,120
Hasn't Ryotsu come in yet?

227
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:34,220
I told him absolutely to come in today.

228
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:36,320
I think he'll be here any moment.

229
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,020
There he is.

230
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:43,900
That's unusual, he messed up.

231
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:45,476
It's been happening a lot lately,

232
00:16:45,526 --> 00:16:49,140
missing grabbing documents
or not reaching things.

233
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,020
This time he looks like he's fine.

234
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,100
So close.

235
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:56,600
What is that idiot doing?
Hurry up and get in here!

236
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,100
He's awfully slow.

237
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:08,660
Good morning.

238
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,440
I'm exhausted.

239
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:15,940
What's with that body?

240
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:19,840
Well, actually, once I realized
I wouldn't have to move around,

241
00:17:19,840 --> 00:17:22,700
I really stopped leaving the house.

242
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,980
Before I knew it, I'd turned into this.

243
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,440
Thanks for the meal.

244
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:29,440
You're way too lazy, you idiot!

245
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:32,380
From today on, you're not Gomu Gomu anymore.
You're Debu Jibu Ros.

246
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:38,600
Thief! It's a thief! Catch him!

247
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:39,980
Let's go!

248
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:40,580
Yes!

249
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:46,400
Such a hassle. I'll just stay on standby.

250
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,380
You're coming too!

251
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:51,280
No way! Catch them yourself!

252
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:53,560
Fast!

253
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:55,860
Come on, hurry up and run, run!

254
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:58,800
Help me, Chief!

255
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,100
Are you getting on with it?

256
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:02,620
They're getting away!

257
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,300
Damn it!

258
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:13,240
Could this be a Rubber-Rubber Missile?

259
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:20,000
Heavy?

260
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:21,520
You're under arrest!

261
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:25,125
That's less a missile than

262
00:18:25,175 --> 00:18:27,120
a Rubber-Rubber shot put.

263
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:36,580
You've been slacking off every day, and
that's why your body has become like this.

264
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,620
Try reflecting on that a little.

265
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:43,860
But Chief, these are such convenient powers.

266
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:47,520
Shut up! Look at you,
all puffed up and bloated like this.

267
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:52,380
Listen, from today on,
I will never let you laze around again.

268
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:57,160
I'll work you to the bone until that flab falls off,
so be prepared.

269
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:57,900
Now listen!

270
00:18:58,520 --> 00:18:59,580
No way!

271
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,580
Kōen-mae Police Box, how can I help you?

272
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:08,460
Yes, understood.
We're on our way right away.

273
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:09,572
Chief,

274
00:19:09,622 --> 00:19:14,140
a wanted car thief seems to
have fled somewhere nearby.

275
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,340
The car is a red foreign make.

276
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:18,740
Understood. Everyone, move out.

277
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:21,640
If you spot it, contact me by radio.

278
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:23,100
Roger!

279
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,120
You go too!

280
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:29,840
Yes!

281
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:34,920
Right, what's all this
"chubby Ryotsu" business?

282
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:38,940
Now I'll earn some merit and
show up the Chief and the others!

283
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:42,420
That must be the car.

284
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:43,940
Like hell I'll let him get away!

285
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:46,280
Rubber rope!

286
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,680
What do you think you're doing, you idiot?

287
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:06,840
Chief, the suspect is just up ahead!

288
00:20:06,840 --> 00:20:09,820
I've got hold of the suspect's car bumper,

289
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,720
so just follow my arm and you'll see.

290
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:14,980
Got it! Don't you dare let go of that hand,
even if you die!

291
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:16,240
I know, I know.

292
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,360
Catch this guy and redeem your honor!

293
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:25,840
Why is he driving through a place like this?

294
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:29,980
Looks like the suspect
squeezed through on two wheels.

295
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,560
Smart aleck!

296
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:35,380
Chief, what am I supposed to do?

297
00:20:35,380 --> 00:20:37,460
Stay right there and don't move for now.

298
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:39,560
But whatever you do,
don't let go of that hand!

299
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:40,660
No way...

300
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:47,360
Hey, how far does he plan to run?

301
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:57,980
Just one step short,

302
00:20:58,340 --> 00:21:01,700
so they were selling
the stolen cars overseas?

303
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:04,800
Overseas?

304
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:13,420
I've had enough!

305
00:21:13,920 --> 00:21:16,820
Stay like this until we catch the culprit?

306
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:18,460
You've got to be kidding me!

307
00:21:18,460 --> 00:21:19,680
I'm letting go now!

308
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:21,160
I'm letting you go, got it?

309
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,100
Chooryaah!

310
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:29,340
My hands won't come back. Why?

311
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:35,340
W-what, Brazil?!

312
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:40,040
Looks like the car theft ring
was selling the cars overseas.

313
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:44,940
When we checked the cargo ship's destination,
we found it was bound for Brazil.

314
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:47,140
Th-then what about my hands?

315
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:50,220
They're probably under
the Brazilian sky by now.

316
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:54,320
What am I supposed to do?

317
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:58,540
Senpai, have you lost some weight?

318
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,420
Your double chin's gone, too.

319
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:04,400
Huh?

320
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,160
Chief!

321
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,400
He hasn't eaten anything for a while,
you know.

322
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,600
He's lost his flab,
so he's being pulled along.

323
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,025
Hey,

324
00:22:15,075 --> 00:22:18,720
If he zooms off now,
who knows where he'll end up.

325
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:20,447
Nakagawa, Chief,

326
00:22:20,497 --> 00:22:23,460
Please, don't let go!

327
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,340
Nakagawa, the rope!

328
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:27,900
Bring the tow rope from the window side!

329
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:28,480
Yes!

330
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:32,540
Chief! Help me!

331
00:22:32,540 --> 00:22:36,100
N-Nakagawa's coming soon!
You stepped on it too, didn't you!

332
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:37,040
Y-yes!

333
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:44,600
C-Chief! Senpai!

334
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,300
Ryotsu! Don't drag me into this too!

335
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:52,600
It was you, Chief,
who told me not to let go!

336
00:23:07,180 --> 00:23:08,060
Help!

337
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:10,520
What?

338
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,100
What!?

339
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:32,920
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

340
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:36,820
Answer me, you Rare-Arts-Ar!

341
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:43,640
I won't eat picked-up nuts anymore, I swear.

342
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:45,620
Somebody help me.

343
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:51,160
Damn you, Dragon Warrior!

344
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,080
How dare you cancel my Robo Deka Bancho!

345
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:56,580
In that case,
I'll launch my own manga magazine

346
00:23:56,580 --> 00:23:58,920
and crush Weekly Sapphire!

347
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:01,380
Who'll draw the manga?

348
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:03,700
I've got a great idea.

349
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:07,520
Next time: Ryotsu-Style Manga School.
See you then!

